{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And I will make you a great nation, etc.</b> Since He commanded him three things, He set for him, corresponding to them, three: <b>ואעשׂך</b> (And I will make you), etc., corresponding to ״לך לך מארצך״ (Go you from your land); <b>ואברכך ואגדלה שׁמך</b> (And I will bless you and I will make great your name) corresponding to ״וממולדתך״ (and from your birthplace); <b>והיה ברכה</b> (And be a blessing) corresponding to ״ומבית אביך״ (and from your father's house). For you find that when a person is in his land, among his family and his father's house, he has three things: first, that he has many acquaintances, friends, and lovers; second, that the members of his family crown him with splendor, honor, and majesty, as is the way of every family toward the children of its family; third, that he is sustained, provided for, and shown compassion from his father's house for his needs. And when he leaves his land, etc., he lacks all of these. Therefore HaShem said to him, corresponding to ״מארצך״ (from your land): I will make for you many lovers, more than those who issue from your loins. And corresponding to the loss of the benefit of the family members, as mentioned — ״ואברכך ואגדלה שׁמך״ (And I will bless you and I will make great your name). And corresponding to the loss of the one who benefits him from his father's house — ״והיה ברכה״ (And be a blessing)."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:31.691722955Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}